Variables are the named memory locations which hold some values.
JavaScript is dynamically  typed which means that here we need not to specify the data-type of the variable.
The data-types of the data being stored is automatically determined. 

Variables can be declared with the help of three keywords which are, var, let and const.
These different ways of declaring variables differ on the basis of their scope and ability to reinitialize in a program. 

var was used most commonly but it is less commonly used today because,
var can be accessed under a function or globally in the program. let and const can be used under the block of code where it is declared.
var and let can be reinitialize with a new value in the program while const cannot be reinitialize. The value assigned to it stays constant.
A variable declared with var keyword can be redeclared while a variable declared with let or const cannot be redeclared.
var and let are not required to initialize with an initial value while const requires an initial value to be decalred.
